WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.734
-Enjoy yourself.
Welcome, welcome, welcome

00:00:02.734 --> 00:00:04.701
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.701 --> 00:00:07.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.934 --> 00:00:10.200
Thank you all for being here.
Today is Monday.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.567
There are so many great days
of the week.

00:00:12.567 --> 00:00:14.300
♪ Monday, Tuesday,
Wednesday, Thursday ♪

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:15.901
♪ Friday, Saturday, Sunday,
Monday... ♪

00:00:15.901 --> 00:00:18.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:18.334 --> 00:00:20.501
There's a lot of buzz
in the building right now,

00:00:20.501 --> 00:00:23.434
also in New York City, 'cause
Jungkook is here tonight.

00:00:23.434 --> 00:00:25.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:29.334 --> 00:00:31.667
And, also, yesterday was
the New York City Marathon.

00:00:31.667 --> 00:00:33.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.367
Anyone here run the marathon?

00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:39.033
[ Scattered cheers ]

00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:41.367
There's probably more.
They're just too tired to clap.

00:00:41.367 --> 00:00:43.000
It's just --
Running a marathon is weird

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:44.601
because yesterday
you were a superhero.

00:00:44.601 --> 00:00:46.267
Today you need help
getting out of a chair.

00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:48.734
You know what I'm saying? I love
the New York City Marathon.

00:00:48.734 --> 00:00:50.400
It's the only time
you can brag about

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.834
finishing in 34,000th place.

00:00:52.834 --> 00:00:54.501
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.501 --> 00:00:56.133
But this is cool --
the winner of the marathon

00:00:56.133 --> 00:00:57.601
set a new course record

00:00:57.601 --> 00:01:00.467
of 2 hours, 4 minutes,
and 58 seconds.

00:01:00.467 --> 00:01:02.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:06.467 --> 00:01:08.667
Everyone was like,
"Okay -- you and only you

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:10.434
are allowed to post
on Instagram.

00:01:10.434 --> 00:01:12.601
No one else."

00:01:12.601 --> 00:01:14.667
Meanwhile, the big news is that,
according to a new poll,

00:01:14.667 --> 00:01:17.033
former President Trump
is leading President Biden

00:01:17.033 --> 00:01:19.300
in five swing states.

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:20.601
Has a lot of people talking.

00:01:20.601 --> 00:01:22.100
Here. Take a look
at this whole thing.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:24.267
When asked who should
be president in 2024,

00:01:24.267 --> 00:01:26.534
15% said Donald Trump,

00:01:26.534 --> 00:01:28.868
10% said Joe Biden,

00:01:28.868 --> 00:01:33.133
74% said, "No, we are
absolutely not doing this.

00:01:33.133 --> 00:01:34.534
Absolutely not.

00:01:34.534 --> 00:01:36.601
The election is 364 days away.

00:01:36.601 --> 00:01:40.200
So take your little poll
and lose my number.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.234
I don't have
the mental energy for this.

00:01:43.234 --> 00:01:44.934
Honestly, I'm just
trying to make it

00:01:44.934 --> 00:01:47.834
to Thursday's
'Golden Bachelor.'

00:01:47.834 --> 00:01:49.801
I'm not deciding
between Trump and Biden

00:01:49.801 --> 00:01:53.200
before Gary decides between
Theresa and Faith.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:54.901
They both have
such a zest for life.

00:01:54.901 --> 00:01:57.200
I don't know
what Gary's going to do.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.067
All I know is that
he's proven that love

00:01:59.067 --> 00:02:01.100
doesn't have an expiration date.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:02.968
Which is a nice way of saying

00:02:02.968 --> 00:02:06.334
you can still get freaky-deaky
in your 70s."

00:02:06.334 --> 00:02:09.801
And finally,
1% said Ron DeSantis.

00:02:09.801 --> 00:02:12.133
So, we have
a whole year of this.

00:02:12.133 --> 00:02:14.367
We have a whole year
of all of this.

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:16.601
I'm not ready.

00:02:16.601 --> 00:02:19.300
That's right. New polling shows
that Trump leads Biden

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:22.267
